SOURCE PACKET
{"id": "FL-018-N1", "type": "field_note"}
Gateway GW-18 uses a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B with default thermal settings. During this observation the SoC temperature rose to 82 degrees Celsius and the Arm clock decreased. The GPU clock was not measured. No maintenance or parts use was recorded.

{"id": "FL-018-N2", "type": "public_reference_summary"}
Raspberry Pi thermal guidance: in the 80–85 °C range, Arm cores are progressively throttled. At 85 °C, both Arm cores and the GPU are throttled. This describes thermal-management behavior, not evidence that a repair was performed.

